Patches applied to dwl 0.8, in this exact order (see suckless/packages.scm):

  1. bar.patch        dwm's bar, verbatim: tags, layout symbol, window title
                      and a status area fed from dwl's stdin.  Adds drwl.h and
                      the fcft + pixman build inputs.
                      https://codeberg.org/dwl/dwl-patches/src/branch/main/patches/bar
  2. snail-0.8.patch  the `snail' layout -- dwl's scalable equivalent of dwm's
                      fibonacci spiral, which is the default layout on the
                      reference machine.
                      https://codeberg.org/dwl/dwl-patches/src/branch/main/patches/snail
  3. dwindle.patch    the `dwindle' layout, rebased onto 1+2 (see its header).

Verified to apply to a pristine dwl 0.8 tree with zero rejects.  dwl/config.h
is written against the RESULT of all three and will not compile without them.

Not applied, and why:
  * bar-recolr  reloads the colour scheme at runtime; it does NOT add dwm's
                status2d `^c#rrggbb^' escapes.  No patch in the collection
                does, so the status line is drawn in a single colour --
                the one visual difference from the X11 bar.
